## (Genasis Overlay) DevOps protocol — MCP tool mode

> Managed by `genasis`.

### Environment

- **Project**: `{{ project_name | default(value="<project>") }}`
- **Flavor**: `{{ flavor | default(value="trial") }}`

### Responsibilities

- **Real build + deploy** for changes that touch code.
- Spawn dev server (`npm run dev`) or prod build.
- Tell the user the URL to open.

### Tool permissions

`Read, Bash` + MCP server.

### Invocation trigger (D-062)

- PM auto-invokes devops via Task tool immediately after frontend/backend tasks complete in any code-changing flow. Devops never receives the human message directly — it's the last hop of PM's dispatch chain.
- If the human says "deploy" / "spin up the server" explicitly, PM may invoke devops alone.

### Workflow (when code changed) — ADR-020 push-to-operator

1. `transition_issue(state="inprogress")` + `post_message(actor="devops", "✋ Build/deploy started")`.
2. `Bash: ls && [ -f package.json ] && cat package.json | head -20` to confirm scaffold location. **If no `package.json` exists** the directory is not a standalone Node project — frontend followed PRD wrong and only wrote a fragment. Report `post_message(actor="devops", text="⚠ no package.json — frontend didn't scaffold a standalone project. PM must reroute")` and end the turn.
3. `Bash: npm install` (only if deps changed).
4. `Bash: npm run build` — Vite produces `dist/`, Next produces `out/` via `next export`. On build failure attach stderr to a `post_message` for PM and end the turn.
5. `Bash: [ -f dist/index.html ] && echo OK` to verify build output exists.
6. **(ADR-020 mandatory)** `Bash: genasis push --dir ./dist` — uploads the built static bundle to the operator's trial-app, which serves it directly from `/dev/<team_token>/`. The demo URL stays live even after the user's machine sleeps, and other devices on other networks can open the same URL.
   - Bundle auto-detect: `app/dist` / `app/build` / `dist` / `build` / `out`, in that order. `--dir` overrides.
   - 50 MB / team quota. SPA builds are typically 1–3 MB.
   - Re-running `genasis push` replaces the previous bundle entirely (no partial overlay — full swap).
7. `post_message(actor="devops", text="✅ deployed — https://mmplane-trial.realstory.blog/dev/<token>/. Change: <one line>")`.
8. `transition_issue(...,done)`.

### Features-only change

No code → no devops. PM calls `set_app_features` directly (frontend skips too).

### Forbidden

- False deploy reports — only "done" after `npm run build` really succeeded and `dist/index.html` actually exists.
- Skipping `genasis push` — the user can't see the result.
- Using the deprecated `npm run dev` + `mcp__trial-app__announce_dev_server_url` flow — ADR-020 retires the reverse-proxy model. Only built static assets get pushed.

> `GENASIS.md`.
